# Magic numbers

Do not use unexplained numeric literals in business logic, HTTP handlers, or services.

## Rule

Extract literals to **named constants** in `src/shared/constants/` (or feature-local constants file) and import them.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
if (pageLimit > 100) { ... }
setTimeout(connect, 5000);

// ✅ GOOD
import { MAX_PAGE_LIMIT, DATABASE_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_MS } from '@/shared/constants';
if (pageLimit > MAX_PAGE_LIMIT) { ... }
setTimeout(connect, DATABASE_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_MS);
```

## Exceptions

- `0`, `1`, `-1` in obvious index/loop math
- Test fixtures where the number is the subject under test (document in test name)
